<setup>
<selectFromSequence name="a" from="-7" to="-3"/>
<selectFromSequence name="b" from="2" to="6"/>
<selectFromSequence name="c" from="-3" to="3" exclude="0"/>
<function name="f">
    $a*x + $b
  </function>
  <derivative name="fP">$f</derivative>
</setup>

  <p>
    Consider the function <m>f(x) = $f</m>.  We are going to use the limit definition of the derivative to determine a formula for <m>f'(x)</m>.

    <ol marker="a.">
      <li>
        <p>
          Recall that the limit definition of <m>f'(x)</m> is
          <me> f'(x) = \lim_{h \to 0} \frac{f(x+h)-f(x)}{h} </me>
          and thus we need to determine expressions for <m>f(x+h)</m> and <m>f(x+h) - f(x)</m>.
        </p>

        <p>Using the given formula <m>f(x) = $f</m>,
      which of the following is the simplest possible expression for <m>f(x+h)</m>?
            <answer>
              <choiceInput><shortDescription>simplest possible expression for f of x plus h</shortDescription>
                <choice><m>f(x+h)=  <math simplify> -$a*x + $b + $a*h</math></m>  </choice>
                <choice><m>f(x+h)=  <math simplify> $a*x + $b - $a*h</math></m>  </choice>
                <choice><m>f(x+h) = $a(x-h) + $b </m></choice>
                <choice credit="1"><m>f(x+h)=  <math simplify> $a*x + $b + $a*h</math></m>  </choice>
              </choiceInput>
            </answer>
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
      <p>Which of the following is the simplest possible expression for <m>f(x+h) - f(x)</m>?
            <answer>
              <choiceInput><shortDescription>simplest possible expression for f of x plus h minus f of x</shortDescription>
                <choice><m>f(x+h) - f(x) = $a(x+h) + $b - (<math simplify="numbers">$a*x+$b</math>) </m></choice>
                <choice credit="1"><m>f(x+h) - f(x) =  <math simplify>$a*h </math></m>  </choice>
                <choice><m>f(x+h) - f(x) =  <math simplify>-$a*h </math></m>  </choice>
                <choice><m>f(x+h) - f(x) =  <math simplify>$a*h + 2*$b </math></m>  </choice>
              </choiceInput>
            </answer>
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Next, apply the limit definition of the derivative by substituting the simplest possible expression for <m>f(x+h)-f(x)</m> in the space provided:
        </p>
        <p>
      <answer><mathInput name="dq_x1" minWidth="20" prefill="/h"><label><m>f'(x)= \displaystyle \lim_{h \to 0} \frac{f(x+h)-f(x)}{h} = \lim_{h \to 0} </m> </label></mathInput>
        <award symbolicEquality><when>$dq_x1 =
        ($a*h)/h
      </when></award>
        <award credit="0" name="notsimplified" symbolicEquality simplifyOnCompare="full" expandOnCompare><when>$dq_x1 =
        ($$f(x+h) - $$f(x))/h
      </when></award>
        <award credit="0" name="toosimplified"><when>$dq_x1 =
        ($$f(x+h) - $$f(x))/h
      </when></award>
      </answer></p>
        <feedback condition="$notsimplified">Your numerator is not simplified enough, yet.</feedback>
        <feedback condition="$toosimplified">Don't divide by <m>h</m> until the next answer box. Leave this answer with a numerator divided by <m>h</m>.</feedback>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>Simplifying the difference quotient in part (c) as much as possible, we see that</p>
        <p>
      <answer><mathInput name="simp_x1"><label><m>f'(x)= \displaystyle \lim_{h \to 0} </m> </label></mathInput>
        <award symbolicEquality><when>$simp_x1 =
          $a
        </when></award>
        <award name="notsimplified2" credit="0"><when>$simp_x1 =
          $a
        </when></award>
      </answer></p>
        <feedback condition="$notsimplified2">Your answer is not simplified enough, yet.</feedback>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>Finally, evaluating the limit by letting <m>h \to 0</m>, we determine the value of <m>f'(x)</m>:</p>
        <p> <answer symbolicEquality><label><m>f'(x) = </m></label>$$fP(x)</answer></p>
      </li>

    </ol>
  </p>